It would take a long time for me to go through all these figures, because it is quite a table, but I will take the tax alone and read a few figures to the house which will leave no doubt as to the very carefully worked out progressive character of these increases in income taxation.
Let us take a single man having an income of $700. The percentage of the increase in tax to what he has left after his present taxation is a minus quantity, minus 2 per cent; that is a decrease. At $850, the increase in the tax is -1 per cent; at $1,000, the increase is -4 per cent; at $1,250, the increase is -4 per cent; at $1,500, the increase is 2-3 per cent; at $1,750, the increase is 3-9 per cent; at $2,000, the increase is 6 per cent; at $2,500, the increase is 7-5 per cent; at $3,000, the increase is 8-8 per cent; at $4,000, the increase is 10-4 per cent; at $5,000, the increase is 10-7 per cent;

